You can consult details how to use git in 
https://qiita.com/kohga/items/dccf135b0af395f69144

reduce_D02 in txcalv deteriorates the convergence if it is activated.


=== Check changes in a local repository ===

Confirm which files have been modified and should be uploaded.
$ git status

=== Changes in the remote repository are reflected in the local repository. ===

$ git pull

=== Update via git ===

Specify the file which will be uploaded.
$ git add hoge
During this procedure, the status which "git status" shows is being updated.

The file is commited to the HEAD in my local (not remote) repository. 
$ git commit -m "message"

Send those files to my remote repository.
$ git push origin txnew


=== Reflect modified and deleted files ===

$ git add -u
$ git commit -m "message"
$ git push


=== See what files managed ===

$ git ls-files

=== Remove files ===

$ git rm hoge


------------------------------------------------------------------------

TX calculation would be broken up if you use "eqdsk.dat".
It will not happen when you use "eqdata_circular".

The namelist given as
 &tx
  ieqread=2
  zeffin=2

  isupg8=0
  igbdf=0
 /
could let computation work even if
 &txequ
  eqfile='eqdsk.dat'
 /
The numerical oscillations appear near the boundary.

The namelist given as
 &tx
  ieqread=2
  zeffin=2

  isupg8=1
  supgstab=0.5
 /
could also let computation work regardless of the value of igbdf.

cf.
txnew_20200115 --> OK (not including impurities)
txnew_20200602 --> OK (not including impurities) --> isupg2=0
txnew_20200622 --> NG (not including impurities) --> isupg2=1
txnew_20200629 --> Not working ...
txnew_20200721 --> NG (including impurities)
